WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:03.700
<v Board member>Who knew the interlock had been bypassed?

2
00:00:04.342 --> 00:00:11.578
<v Narrator>At Delta Industrial Nigeria's Ogun State facility, pressure to hit group margin targets had been building for months.

3
00:00:12.228 --> 00:00:15.753
<v Operator>That interlock has been bypassed for months. We shouldn't be running this line.

4
00:00:16.003 --> 00:00:19.528
<v Supervisor>I've raised it. The answer is keep running. Just get this batch through.

5
00:00:19.870 --> 00:00:23.870
[Alarm. Machinery stops abruptly. Shouting.]

6
00:00:24.212 --> 00:00:26.699
<v Plant Manager>What exactly do you want in the incident report?

7
00:00:26.949 --> 00:00:29.712
<v Regional Director>Stick to what's confirmed. Don't put conclusions in writing yet.

8
00:00:30.154 --> 00:00:35.431
<v Narrator>As the first reports came in, it became clear the accident might not be an isolated safety failure.

9
00:00:38.031 --> 00:00:41.731
<v Auditor>I've gone back fourteen months. Three payments, all through the same agent.

10
00:00:42.831 --> 00:00:43.931
<v Finance Manager>They're expediting fees.

11
00:00:44.631 --> 00:00:46.731
<v Auditor>Then why is there no record of where the money actually went?

12
00:00:47.173 --> 00:00:51.673
<v Journalist>Workers say safety concerns were raised before the fatality. Will the company comment?

13
00:00:52.215 --> 00:00:56.715
<v FISCA official>We're aware of the fatality. We have not opened an inquiry — at this stage.

14
00:00:57.257 --> 00:01:01.880
<v Narrator>Questions about safety, oversight and financial conduct were beginning to converge.

15
00:01:02.680 --> 00:01:09.180
<v Managing Director>The Board meets in seventy-two hours. I need to understand what happened, how far this goes, and what we can defend.

16
00:01:09.722 --> 00:01:15.757
<v Narrator>You will examine the evidence, determine where accountability lies, and advise the Board on what Delta should do next.

17
00:01:16.657 --> 00:01:19.357
You have 72 hours.

